#prob(title: [Curtis 7.8])[
    Spacecraft $A$ and $B$ are in the same circular earth orbit with a period of #qty(2, "h"). $B$ is #qty(6, "km") ahead of $A$. At $t = 0$, $B$ applies an in-track $Delta v$ (retrofire) of #qty(3, "m/s"). Using a CW frame attached to $A$, determine the distance between $A$ and $B$ at $t = qty(30, "min")$ and the velocity of $B$ relative to $A$ at that instant.
] <hwk:p03>

In the CW frame attached to $A$, the mean motion and elapsed angle are:
$
      n & = (2 pi)/T = (2 pi)/qty(7200, "s") = qty(result("03", "n"), "rad/s"), \
    n t & = (2 pi)/qty(2, "h") dot qty(30, "min") = pi/2.
$

Since $A$ and $B$ share the same circular orbit, $B$ is stationary in $A$'s CW frame before the burn: $delta vbu(r)_0 = 6 vuu(j) space (unit("km"))$ and $delta vbu(v)_0^(-) = vb(0)$. Indeed, with $delta x_0 = 0$ and $delta vbu(v)_0 = vb(0)$, #link(<eqn:cw>)[the CW solution] gives $delta vbu(r) (t) = delta vbu(r)_0$ for all $t$.

The retrofire acts opposite to the direction of motion ($-vuu(j)$), so immediately after the burn:
$
    delta vbu(v)_0^(+) = delta vbu(v)_0^(-) + Delta vbu(v) = -3 vuu(j) space (unit("m/s")) = -0.003 vuu(j) space (unit("km/s")).
$

With $delta x_0 = 0$ and $delta dot(x)_0^(+) = 0$, only the second columns of #link(<eqn:cw-stm>)[the state transition matrices] contribute. The second column of $Phi_(v r)$ is zero, so $delta y_0$ does not affect the relative velocity. At $n t = pi/2$, where $sin(n t) = 1$ and $cos(n t) = 0$:
$
    delta x & = (2(1 - cos(n t)))/n delta dot(y)_0^(+) = (qty(result("03", "Phi_rv_12"), "s")) (qty(-0.003, "km/s")) = qty(result("03", "dr_x"), "km"), \
    delta y & = delta y_0 + (4 sin(n t) - 3 n t)/n delta dot(y)_0^(+) \
    & = qty(6, "km") + (qty(result("03", "Phi_rv_22"), "s")) (qty(-0.003, "km/s")) = qty(result("03", "dr_y"), "km"), \
    delta dot(x) & = 2 sin(n t) delta dot(y)_0^(+) = 2 (qty(-3, "m/s")) = qty(-6, "m/s"), \
    delta dot(y) & = (4 cos(n t) - 3) delta dot(y)_0^(+) = -3 (qty(-3, "m/s")) = qty(9, "m/s"),
$
with $delta z = delta dot(z) = 0$.

Thus, the distance between $A$ and $B$ at $t = qty(30, "min")$ is:
$
    d = abs(delta vbu(r)) = sqrt(delta x^2 + delta y^2) = qty(result("03", "distance"), "km") quad qed
$

The velocity of $B$ relative to $A$ (measured in the CW frame) at that instant is:
$
    delta vbu(v) & = -6 vuu(i) + 9 vuu(j) space (unit("m/s")), \
    abs(delta vbu(v)) & = sqrt(6^2 + 9^2) space unit("m/s") = qty(result("03", "speed"), "m/s") quad qed
$

#figure(
    image("../outputs/figures/s03.png", width: 60%),
    caption: [Motion of $B$ relative to $A$ after the retrofire, with the relative velocity at $t = qty(30, "min")$.],
)
<hwk:s03>

