    For an ellipse, $chi = sqrt(a) Delta E$, which matches the value above. With $vbu(r)_i$, $dot(vbu(r))_i$ the initial and final states and $I$ the identity, the blocks are (Eqs. 46--49):
    $
        A & = r_2/mu (dot(vbu(r))_2 - dot(vbu(r))_1)(dot(vbu(r))_2 - dot(vbu(r))_1)^TT + 1/r_1^3 [r_1 (1 - f) vbu(r)_2 vbu(r)_1^TT + overline(C) dot(vbu(r))_2 vbu(r)_1^TT] + f I, \
        B & = r_1/mu (1 - f) [(vbu(r)_2 - vbu(r)_1) dot(vbu(r))_1^TT - (dot(vbu(r))_2 - dot(vbu(r))_1) vbu(r)_1^TT] + overline(C)/mu dot(vbu(r))_2 dot(vbu(r))_1^TT + g I, \
        C & = -1/r_1^2 (dot(vbu(r))_2 - dot(vbu(r))_1) vbu(r)_1^TT - 1/r_2^2 vbu(r)_2 (dot(vbu(r))_2 - dot(vbu(r))_1)^TT - (mu overline(C))/(r_1^3 r_2^3) vbu(r)_2 vbu(r)_1^TT \
