        D & = r_1/mu (dot(vbu(r))_2 - dot(vbu(r))_1)(dot(vbu(r))_2 - dot(vbu(r))_1)^TT + 1/r_2^3 [r_1 (1 - f) vbu(r)_2 vbu(r)_1^TT - overline(C) vbu(r)_2 dot(vbu(r))_1^TT] + dot(g) I.
    $

    Thus, the two-body state transition matrix over #qty(30, "min") is $Phi = mat(A, B; C, D)$ with:
    $
        A & = resultMat("05b", "A"), & B & = resultMat("05b", "B") space (unit("s")), \
        C & = resultMat("05b", "C") times 10^(-3) space (unit("/s")), & quad D & = resultMat("05b", "D") quad qed
    $

    As checks, central differences of the #link(<eqn:s05-lagrange>)[part (a)] propagation (#qty(1, "m") and #qty(1, "mm/s") steps) match $Phi$ to a relative $#num(resultRaw("05b", "finite difference error"))$. $Phi$ is also symplectic, $Phi^TT J Phi = J$ to $#num(resultRaw("05b", "symplectic error"))$ with $J = mat(0, I; -I, 0)$, so $det(Phi) = #result("05b", "det")$.
